.TH RDW 1 "2025" "rdw" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rdw \- pipe process output into a live browser layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rdw
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rdw
is a self-contained daemon that receives output from one or more processes and
displays it in a live multi-pane browser layout.
.PP
Any process that writes to its standard output can pipe that output to
.B rdw pipe
and have it appear in a named pane in the browser in real time.
The server embeds a complete single-page application; no external assets,
network access, or CDN are required.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
TCP port to connect to or listen on (default: 7681).
Every command accepts this flag to address a specific server instance when
multiple servers are running simultaneously.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Server management
.TP
.B rdw server start
Start the server. Options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
TCP port to listen on (default 7681).
.TP
.B \-\-open\-browser
Open the browser UI immediately after the server starts.
.TP
.B \-\-kv\-persist \fIPATH\fR
Enable SQLite KV persistence at \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Load the persisted KV store from the SQLite database on startup.
Requires \fB\-\-kv\-persist\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auth
Disable token authentication. Development use only.
.RE
.TP
.B rdw server stop
Stop the running server.
.TP
.B rdw server list
List all running rdw server instances.
.SS Piping process output
.TP
.B rdw pipe \-\-id \fITARGET_ID\fR
Read lines from the piped process output and relay them to the pane identified
by \fITARGET_ID\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-id \fITARGET_ID\fR
Destination pane identifier (required).
Pattern: \fI[a-zA-Z0-9_][a-zA-Z0-9_ -]*\fR, max 64 characters.
.TP
.B \-\-layout \fINAME\fR|\fIPATH\fR
Apply the named layout preset or on-disk layout file before streaming begins.
.TP
.B \-\-window \fINAME\fR
Route the stream into a specific window.
.TP
.B \-\-forward rd|rdw|both
Also forward the stream to bash-rd (\fBrd\fR), rdw only, or both.
.TP
.B \-\-forward\-to\-file \fIPATH\fR
Mirror the stream to a file or FIFO simultaneously.
.TP
.B \-\-forward\-to\-cmd \fICMD\fR
Mirror the stream as standard input to a shell command simultaneously.
.RE
.SS Window management
.TP
.B rdw window create \fINAME\fR
Create a new window.
.TP
.B rdw window close \fINAME\fR
Close a window. Blocked if it is the last window in the session.
.TP
.B rdw window rename \fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR
Rename a window.
.TP
.B rdw window focus \fINAME\fR
Switch the browser view to the named window.
.TP
.B rdw window list
List all windows and their panes.
.SS Pane management
.TP
.B rdw pane split \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-dir h|v\fR]
Split an existing pane horizontally or vertically.
.TP
.B rdw pane resize \fIID\fR \fISIZE\fR
Resize a pane.
\fISIZE\fR is \fIN\fR (columns/rows), \fINpx\fR (pixels), or \fIN%\fR (percentage).
.TP
.B rdw pane zoom \fIID\fR
Toggle full-window zoom on a pane.
.TP
.B rdw pane swap \fIID1\fR \fIID2\fR
Swap the grid positions of two panes.
.TP
.B rdw pane close \fIID\fR
Remove a pane.
.SS KV store
.TP
.B rdw kv set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set a KV entry.
Keys follow \fI[a-zA-Z0-9_][a-zA-Z0-9_ -]*\fR with an optional
\fIwindow:\fR or \fIpane:\fR namespace prefix.
.TP
.B rdw kv get \fIKEY\fR
Print the value of a KV entry.
.TP
.B rdw kv delete \fIKEY\fR
Delete a KV entry.
.TP
.B rdw kv list [\fIPREFIX\fR]
List KV keys, optionally filtered by prefix.
.SS Token management
.TP
.B rdw token create [\fB\-\-scope \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-expires \fIDURATION\fR]
Create an auth token. The plain-text value is printed once only and never
stored. Duration examples: \fB1h\fR, \fB24h\fR, \fB7d\fR.
.TP
.B rdw token revoke \fIID\fR
Revoke a token immediately. Active WebSocket connections using that token
are closed.
.TP
.B rdw token list
List all active tokens.
.SS Layout management
.TP
.B rdw layout apply \fINAME\fR|\fIPATH\fR
Apply a saved or on-disk layout. When \fINAME\fR is given, the server looks
up a previously saved snapshot. When \fIPATH\fR is given, the file is parsed
as a YAML layout spec and sent to the server.
.TP
.B rdw layout save \fINAME\fR
Snapshot the current session layout under \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B rdw layout list
List saved layouts.
.SS Group management
.TP
.B rdw group hide \fINAME\fR
Hide all panes in the named group.
.TP
.B rdw group show \fINAME\fR
Show all panes in the named group.
.TP
.B rdw group focus \fINAME\fR
Focus all panes in the named group.
.TP
.B rdw group kill \fINAME\fR
Close all panes in the named group.
.SS Focus cycle
.TP
.B rdw cycle start \fIWINDOW\fR [\fIWINDOW\fR ...] [\fB\-\-interval\-ms \fIN\fR]
Begin automatic focus rotation through the listed windows at \fIN\fR
milliseconds per window (default 5000).
.TP
.B rdw cycle stop
Stop the running focus cycle.
.SS Export
.TP
.B rdw save \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-pane \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-window \fINAME\fR]
Export scrollback to a Markdown bundle in \fIDIR\fR.
Decoded images are saved under \fIDIR/assets/\fR.
Without \fB\-\-pane\fR or \fB\-\-window\fR, the entire session is exported.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B rdw selftest
Run the 11-check in-process smoke suite. Exits 0 if all pass.
.SH CONTROL SEQUENCES
Lines piped through
.B rdw pipe
that begin with a recognised prefix are intercepted and acted on rather than
displayed in the pane.
.TP
.B v:\fIPAYLOAD\fR
Verbatim passthrough. Strips the prefix and displays \fIPAYLOAD\fR as-is.
Prevents any other prefix on the line from being interpreted.
.TP
.B =:\fIk\fR=\fIv\fR;\fIk2\fR=\fIv2\fR
Write key-value pairs to the session KV store.
.TP
.B f:\fINAME\fR
Switch the pane's content formatter.
Valid names: text, json, yaml, markdown, csv, image.
.TP
.B b64:\fIDATA\fR
Base64-encoded binary data.
Used with the image formatter or saved as an asset on export.
.TP
.B bm:\fINAME\fR
Create a named scrollback bookmark at the current line index.
.TP
.B hl:\fIPROFILE\fR
Apply the named highlight profile to the pane.
Profiles are created via the REST API or
.B rdw
highlight commands.
.TP
.B sc:\fIACTION\fR
Scrollback control.
\fBclear\fR wipes the server-side buffer and all browser views.
\fBtop\fR and \fBbottom\fR scroll the browser view without clearing.
.TP
.B t:
Toggle a line-level RFC-3339 timestamp prefix on subsequent output.
.TP
.B c:
Clear the pane scrollback (alias for sc:clear via legacy prefix).
.SH AUTHENTICATION
All REST API endpoints and WebSocket connections require a Bearer token unless
.B \-\-no\-auth
is set.
Tokens are stored SHA-256 hashed on the server.
The plain-text token is shown exactly once at creation.
.PP
The Unix domain socket at
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rdw/<session_id>.sock
(mode 0600) accepts connections from the owning user without a token.
.B rdw pipe
prefers this path; it falls back to HTTP Bearer token for remote servers.
.PP
The admin endpoint
.I /api/v1/admin/connections
additionally requires a loopback source address regardless of token scope.
Use
.B \-\-network\-expose
to lift this restriction.
.SH LAYOUT FILE FORMAT
Layout files are YAML with the following structure:
.PP
.nf
schema_version: 1
windows:
  - name: STRING
    panes:
      - target_id: STRING
        split: h|v
        size: STRING        # N, Npx, or N%
        group: STRING       # optional group name
        private: BOOL
        scrollback_cap: N
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base directory for the Unix socket.
Defaults to \fI/run/user/<uid>\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the server registry file.
Defaults to \fI$HOME/.cache\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rdw/servers.json
Registry of running rdw instances used by multi-server discovery.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rdw/<id>.sock
Unix socket for the session identified by \fIid\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rdw/config.yaml
Optional configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rd (1)
.PP
Full documentation: https://github.com/nkh/rdw/tree/main/docs
